      "content": "For patients with darker skin tones, the same ABCDE rules can still apply, but it's essential to be aware of skin pigmentation not being a reliable indicator, as melanoma can occur anywhere. Historically, melanoma was more difficult to diagnose in darker skin tones due to the similarity of benign moles and lesions. In recent years, guidelines now recommend using the \"SEVA\" criteria: Symmetry, Evolving, Uncertain, Asymmetry, and A or B (active borders), which is more inclusive for all skin types.",
